2 1.34174Z"></path></svg></a><span class=""><!--[-->   <span></span><span class="relative z-3 font-normal"> Storing Certificates in the Domain Name System (DNS)</span><!--]--></span><!--]--></h3><div class=""><!--[--><div class="md:pr-5 flex-1"><div class="inline-flex w-fit rounded-lg overflow-hidden print:text-sm print:leading-[2] relative z-1 print:m-0 text-xs font-semibold"><!--[--><div class="py-1 uppercase print:text-black print:bg-transparent print:border-1 print:border-black px-2 bg-blue-400 dark:bg-blue-800 text-white print:bg-white"><!--[-->Proposed Standard<!--]--></div><!--]--></div><ul class="relative z-1 hidden lg:block print:block text-base text-gray-800 dark:text-white"><!--[--><li class="inline"><!----><span class="whitespace-nowrap">D. Eastlake 3rd<!--[--><!--]--></span></li><li class="inline"><span class="inline-block mx-2 rotate-45 align-middle print:bg-black print:opacity-100 print-with-background bg-gray-600 dark:bg-white opacity-50 w-[5px] h-[5px]"></span><span class="whitespace-nowrap">O. Gudmundsson<!--[--><!--]--></span></li><!--]--></ul><ul class="relative z-1 hidden lg:block print:block text-base text-gray-800 mt-1 dark:text-white"><!----><!--[--><li class="inline text-[0.9rem] text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-200"><!---->March 1999</li><li class="inline text-[0.9rem] text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-200"><span class="inline-block mx-2 rotate-45 align-middle print:bg-black print:opacity-100 print-with-background bg-gray-600 dark:bg-white opacity-50 w-[5px] h-[5px] align-middle"></span>IETF publication</li><li class="inline text-[0.9rem] text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-200"><span class="inline-block mx-2 rotate-45 align-middle print:bg-black print:opacity-100 print-with-background bg-gray-600 dark:bg-white opacity-50 w-[5px] h-[5px] align-middle"></span>Security Area</li><!--]--></ul><div class="block lg:hidden"><button type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="abstract-rfc-2538" class="relative z-50 text-blue-800 cursor-pointer dark:text-blue-100 underline text-base p-3 -ml-3 -mt-2 -mb-3 print:hidden" aria-label="Show abstract for RFC 2538"><!--[-->Show abstract<!--]--></button><div id="abstract-rfc-2538" class="relative z-50 mt-3 hidden print:block"><h4 id="abstract" class="text-base font-semibold leading-[1.2] text-blue-900 dark:text-gray-300 pt-3 border-t inline-block group"><!----><!--[--> Abstract <!--]--></h4><div class="leading-snug text-gray-800 dark:text-gray-300 text-pretty"><!--[--><p>Cryptographic public key are frequently published and their authenticity demonstrated by certificates.  A CERT resource record (RR) is defined so that such certificates and related certificate revocation lists can be stored in the Domain Name System (DNS). [STANDARDS-TRACK]</p><!--]--></div></div></div><p class="relative z-1 text-red-800 dark:text-red-300 text-base print:text-black"><ul class="inline-block">Obsoleted by <span class="inline-block p-1 -m-1">RFC <b>4398</b></span></ul></p></div><div class="relative z-1 hidden lg:block"><h4 id="abstract" class="text-base font-semibold leading-[1.2] text-blue-900 dark:text-gray-300 inline-block mt-3 pt-2 border-t-1 border-gray-200 group"><!----><!--[--> Abstract <!--]--></h4><div class="pb-2 max-w-[34em] text-black dark:text-white leading-[1.5] text-pretty"><!--[--><p>Cryptographic public key are frequently published and their authenticity demonstrated by certificates.  A CERT resource record (RR) is defined so that such certificates and related certificate revocation lists can be stored in the Domain Name System (DNS). [STANDARDS-TRACK]</p><!--]--></div></div><!--]--></div></div><!----><!--[--><ul class="flex w-fit flex-row -ml-1 -mb-1 gap-4 z-50 py-1 px-1"><li><div class="relative flex flex-col md:flex-row md:gap-2 px-2 py-1"><div class="flex flex-col"><!--[--><button type="button" aria-haspopup="dialog" aria-expanded="false" data-state="closed" class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-center cursor-pointer rounded text-sm text-center md:text-left font-bold ho